---
import PlaygroundShell from '../../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Quorums, outages and zombie deletes" hint="Five nodes, three copies of every row. One or two nodes are down for a long outage, then return. Pick the consistency levels, the repair method and how long deletes are remembered, and count the wrong answers over 2,000 operations.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>The default is <b>QUORUM writes, QUORUM reads, 1 node down, hints and read repair, deletes forgotten after 150 operations</b>. All reads are served, 84 of 987 writes are refused for lack of a second answer, and no read returns an old version of a live row, yet <b>92 of 923</b> checked reads bring back rows that were deleted. The node that was down missed the deletes, and by the time it returned the other replicas had purged their tombstones.</li>
    <li>Set deletes to <b>for the whole run</b>: the zombie rows drop to <b>0</b>, because the tombstone still outranks the old value. Or keep the short memory and choose <b>rebuild the returning node</b>: also <b>0</b>, because the node is wiped and re-streamed instead of trusted.</li>
    <li>Choose <b>ONE and ONE</b> with deletes remembered: almost nothing is refused (985 of 987 writes accepted, 1,013 of 1,013 reads served), but <b>41</b> reads return an old version. Choose <b>2 nodes down</b> with QUORUM and 177 reads are refused, because some rows then have only one live copy.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg wcb" data-wcb>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Write consistency <select class="pg-in" data-w><option value="1">ONE (1 of 3 copies)</option><option value="2" selected>QUORUM (2 of 3)</option><option value="3">ALL (3 of 3)</option></select></label>
      <label>Read consistency <select class="pg-in" data-r><option value="1">ONE (1 of 3 copies)</option><option value="2" selected>QUORUM (2 of 3)</option><option value="3">ALL (3 of 3)</option></select></label>
      <label>Nodes down for the outage <select class="pg-in" data-d><option value="0">0</option><option value="1" selected>1</option><option value="2">2</option></select></label>
      <label>Repair <select class="pg-in" data-rep>
        <option value="none">none</option>
        <option value="hints" selected>hinted handoff and read repair</option>
        <option value="rebuild">hints, read repair and rebuild the returning node</option>
      </select></label>
      <label>Deletes are remembered <select class="pg-in" data-g><option value="150" selected>for 150 operations</option><option value="5000">for the whole run</option></select></label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" data-b1><h3>Writes accepted</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o1></span><span class="pg-note" data-n1></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b2><h3>Reads served</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o2></span><span class="pg-note" data-n2></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b3><h3>Reads of an old version</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o3></span><span class="pg-note" data-n3></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b4><h3>Deleted rows that came back</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o4></span><span class="pg-note" data-n4></span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-out" data-verdict aria-live="polite"></p>
    <p class="pg-note">Model: 5 nodes, each row stored on 3 consecutive nodes, 40 rows, 2,000 operations from a fixed seed (987 writes and deletes, 1,013 reads). Each message to a replica is lost or too slow 10% of the time. The chosen nodes are down from operation 300 to 1,200. A hint is kept for 100 operations, and a hint for a live node is redelivered 10 operations later. Rows 30 to 39 are deleted between operations 500 and 700 and never written again. A write that fails is not judged afterwards, because its outcome is unknown. A read counts as old when it returns a version older than the last acknowledged write, and as a zombie when it returns a live row that was deleted more than the memory ago.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-wcb]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = <T extends HTMLElement>(s: string) => root.querySelector<T>(s)!;
    const OPS = 2000; const KEYS = 40; const N = 5; const BACK = 1200; const FAIL = 300; const HINT_WINDOW = 100; const LOSS = 10;
    type Cell = { ver: number; del: boolean; t: number };
    type Hint = { node: number; key: number; cell: Cell; at: number; exp: number };
    const SEED = 7; const RF = 3; // copies of every row (reps below lists three nodes)
    const WRITE_PCT = 55; const DELETE_FROM = 40; // rolls below 55 write, and from 40 on the write is a delete
    const HOT = { fromKey: 30, from: 500, to: 700, delRoll: 50, readRoll: 99 }; // keys 30+ are deleted during ops 500..699, then only read
    const PICK_SPAN = 6; // random start offset when choosing which live copies a read contacts
    const GC_EVERY = 10; const HINT_DELAY = 10; // ops between tombstone collections; delay before a hint is replayed
    // LCG, upper bits
    let seed = SEED; const rnd = (n: number) => { seed = (seed * 1664525 + 1013904223) % 4294967296; return Math.floor(seed / 65536) % n; };
    // The operations and the random losses are generated once, so every setting faces exactly the same workload.
    const script = Array.from({ length: OPS }, (_, i) => {
      const key = rnd(KEYS); let roll = rnd(100);
      if (key >= HOT.fromKey && i >= HOT.from) roll = i < HOT.to ? HOT.delRoll : HOT.readRoll;
      return { key, roll, lost: [rnd(100), rnd(100), rnd(100)], pick: rnd(PICK_SPAN) };
    });
    function simulate(w: number, r: number, down: number, repair: string, grace: number) {
      const data: Map<number, Cell>[] = Array.from({ length: N }, () => new Map());
      const acked = new Map<number, Cell>(); let hints: Hint[] = [];
      const up = (n: number, i: number) => n >= down || i < FAIL || i >= BACK;
      const reps = (k: number) => [k % N, (k + 1) % N, (k + 2) % N];
      const apply = (n: number, k: number, c: Cell) => { const cur = data[n].get(k); if (!cur || c.ver > cur.ver) data[n].set(k, c); };
      const res = { wOk: 0, wFail: 0, rOk: 0, rFail: 0, checked: 0, stale: 0, zombie: 0 };
      for (let i = 0; i < OPS; i++) {
        if (repair === 'rebuild' && i === BACK) {
          for (let n = 0; n < down; n++) {
            data[n].clear();
            for (let k = 0; k < KEYS; k++) if (reps(k).includes(n)) reps(k).filter((p) => p !== n).forEach((p) => { const c = data[p].get(k); if (c) apply(n, k, c); });
          }
        }
        hints = hints.filter((x) => {
          if (i > x.exp) return false;
          if (x.at <= i && up(x.node, i)) { apply(x.node, x.key, x.cell); return false; }
          return true;
        });
        if (i % GC_EVERY === 0) for (const m of data) for (const [k, c] of Array.from(m)) if (c.del && i - c.t > grace) m.delete(k);
        const op = script[i]; const k = op.key; const rs = reps(k);
        if (op.roll < WRITE_PCT) {
          const cell: Cell = { ver: i + 1, del: op.roll >= DELETE_FROM, t: i }; let acks = 0;
          rs.forEach((n, j) => {
            if (up(n, i) && op.lost[j] >= LOSS) { apply(n, k, cell); acks++; }
            else if (repair !== 'none') hints.push({ node: n, key: k, cell, at: up(n, i) ? i + HINT_DELAY : 0, exp: i + HINT_WINDOW });
          });
          if (acks >= w) { res.wOk++; acked.set(k, cell); } else { res.wFail++; acked.delete(k); }
        } else {
          const live = rs.filter((n) => up(n, i));
          if (live.length < r) { res.rFail++; continue; }
          res.rOk++;
          const start = op.pick % live.length; const contacted = Array.from({ length: r }, (_, j) => live[(start + j) % live.length]);
          let newest: Cell | null = null;
          contacted.forEach((n) => { const c = data[n].get(k); if (c && (!newest || c.ver > newest.ver)) newest = c; });
          if (repair !== 'none' && newest) { const nw = newest; contacted.forEach((n) => apply(n, k, nw)); }
          const a = acked.get(k); if (!a) continue;
          res.checked++;
          const nw = newest as Cell | null;
          let bad: boolean;
          if (!nw) bad = !a.del; else if (nw.ver >= a.ver) bad = false; else bad = !(nw.del && a.del);
          if (bad) { res.stale++; if (a.del && nw && !nw.del && i - a.t > grace) res.zombie++; }
        }
      }
      return res;
    }
    const names = ['', 'ONE', 'QUORUM', 'ALL'];
    const MAX_REFUSED = 0.2; // share of refused writes or reads marked as a problem
    const fmt = (n: number) => n.toLocaleString('en-US');
    function draw() {
      const w = Number(q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-w]').value); const r = Number(q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-r]').value);
      const d = Number(q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-d]').value); const rep = q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-rep]').value; const g = Number(q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-g]').value);
      const x = simulate(w, r, d, rep, g); const writes = x.wOk + x.wFail; const reads = x.rOk + x.rFail;
      q('[data-o1]').textContent = `${fmt(x.wOk)} of ${fmt(writes)}`; q('[data-n1]').textContent = x.wFail ? `${fmt(x.wFail)} refused: fewer than ${w} copies answered` : 'none refused';
      q('[data-o2]').textContent = `${fmt(x.rOk)} of ${fmt(reads)}`; q('[data-n2]').textContent = x.rFail ? `${fmt(x.rFail)} refused: fewer than ${r} live copies` : 'none refused';
      const old = x.stale - x.zombie;
      q('[data-o3]').textContent = `${fmt(old)} of ${fmt(x.checked)}`; q('[data-n3]').textContent = `checked reads of rows with a known last write; W + R = ${w + r}, and ${RF} copies exist`;
      q('[data-o4]').textContent = `${fmt(x.zombie)}`; q('[data-n4]').textContent = 'reads of a row that had been deleted';
      const set = (id: string, bad: boolean) => q<HTMLElement>(id).style.setProperty('--c', bad ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--good)');
      set('[data-b1]', x.wFail > writes * MAX_REFUSED); set('[data-b2]', x.rFail > reads * MAX_REFUSED); set('[data-b3]', old > 0); set('[data-b4]', x.zombie > 0);
      const out = q('[data-verdict]'); const bad = x.zombie > 0 || old > 0 || x.rFail > 0 || x.wFail > writes * MAX_REFUSED; out.classList.toggle('bad', bad);
      const msg: string[] = [];
      if (x.zombie > 0) msg.push(`${fmt(x.zombie)} reads brought back deleted rows. The returning node still held the old values, the other replicas had purged their tombstones after ${g} operations, and no consistency level can outvote a delete that nobody remembers. Remember deletes longer than any outage, or rebuild a node that was down for that long.`);
      if (old > 0) msg.push(`${fmt(old)} reads returned an older version, because ${names[w]} writes and ${names[r]} reads do not have to meet on a common copy (W + R = ${w + r}, which is not more than ${RF}).`);
      if (x.rFail > 0) msg.push(`${fmt(x.rFail)} reads were refused: some rows had fewer than ${r} live copies. Lower consistency would have served them, with the risk of old data.`);
      if (x.wFail > writes * MAX_REFUSED) msg.push(`${fmt(x.wFail)} writes were refused because ${names[w]} needs ${w} answers and some replicas were down or slow.`);
      out.textContent = msg.length ? msg.join(' ') : `No wrong answers in these ${fmt(OPS)} operations${x.wFail ? ` (${fmt(x.wFail)} writes were refused and would be retried)` : ''}. ${w + r > RF ? `W + R = ${w + r} is more than ${RF}, so reads and writes share a copy, and ` : ''}deletes were not forgotten before the returning node was repaired.`;
    }
    root.addEventListener('change', draw);
    draw();
  });
</script>
